.TH RIGORKIT 1 "" "rigorkit" "rigorkit manual"
.SH NAME
rigorkit \- install rigorkit packs and run its helper scripts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
Usage: rigorkit <command> [args]

Commands:
  install [options]      Install packs into your coding agents (same as install.sh)
  script <name> [args]   Run a helper script, custom first, then official
  help [<command>]       Show this list, or the help of one command

Run 'rigorkit help <command>' or 'rigorkit <command> \-\-help' for details.
Manual: man rigorkit. If 'rigorkit' runs an older copy, check which one comes
first in PATH with 'command \-v rigorkit'.
.fi
.SH INSTALL
.nf
Usage: rigorkit install \-\-pack <packs> \-\-agent <agents> [\-\-project <dir> | \-\-global] [options]
       ./install.sh <same options>

Installs packs (skills, agents and, with \-\-global, rules) into each coding
agent's folders. Packs come from this clone and from ~/.rigorkit/custom/packs;
a custom pack replaces the official pack with the same name.

Options:
  \-\-pack <packs>        Comma\-separated packs, or 'all' (official and custom)
  \-\-agent <agents>      Comma\-separated: claude, codex, cursor, opencode
  \-\-project <dir>       Install into a project folder (default: current folder)
  \-\-global              Install into your home folder, including global rules
  \-\-force               Overwrite skills and agents that already exist
  \-\-dry\-run             Print what would change; write nothing
  \-\-uninstall\-rules     Remove rigorkit rule blocks from the global rule files
  \-\-version             Print the version of this clone
  \-\-list                List packs and what each one installs
  \-\-help, \-h            Show this help

Examples:
  rigorkit install \-\-pack core,sdd \-\-agent claude \-\-global
  rigorkit install \-\-pack all \-\-agent claude,codex \-\-project ~/code/app \-\-dry\-run
  rigorkit install \-\-uninstall\-rules \-\-agent claude

Writes:
  <scope>/.claude/skills, <scope>/.agents/skills   skills
  <scope>/.claude/agents, .cursor/agents, .codex/agents, .opencode/agents
                                                  agents (OpenCode global: ~/.config/opencode/agents)
  <scope>/.rigorkit\-version                       installed version
  ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md, ~/.codex/AGENTS.md, ~/.config/opencode/AGENTS.md
                                                  global rules, between rigorkit markers,
                                                  with a <file>.rigorkit.bak backup
  <scope> is the project folder, or your home folder with \-\-global.
.fi
.SH SCRIPT
.nf
Usage: rigorkit script <name> [args]

Runs the first helper script named <name> from, in order:
~/.rigorkit/custom/scripts, the custom packs' scripts folders, and the
official packs' scripts folders not replaced by a custom pack (packs in
name order). Every argument after <name> is passed to the script unchanged,
and rigorkit exits with the script's status.

Options:
  \-\-help                Show this help (only as the first argument)

Examples:
  rigorkit script test\-summary npm test
  rigorkit script json\-peek package.json 2

Writes:
  Nothing; the script itself may write.

Exit status: 2 for a missing or invalid name, 127 when no script has that
name, 126 when the script found first is not executable.
.fi
.SH HELP
.nf
Usage: rigorkit help [<command>]

Shows the list of commands, or the help of one command.

Options:
  \-\-help, \-h            Show this help

Examples:
  rigorkit help
  rigorkit help install

Writes:
  Nothing.
.fi
